        'The symptom-limited threshold concept applies to cognitive work as reliably as to physical work. The same 24-hour rule applies: a cognitive session that provokes symptoms during or in the 24 hours following it exceeded the athlete\'s current capacity. Gradual extension of cognitive task duration and complexity — mirroring the physical load build — is correct RTL and RTW management.',
        '### The Five-Stage Return-to-Learn Progression',
        'For student-athletes, the following cognitive-pacing ladder mirrors the physical GRTS structure:',
        '   - Stage 1: activities of daily living that do not provoke symptoms — brief periods of light reading or screen time, no academic demands.',
        '   - Stage 2: school activities at home — homework in short bursts (15–20 minutes) increasing to 30–60 minutes with planned rest breaks, before returning to school.',
        '   - Stage 3: return to school part-time — reduced school day or selected classes; accommodations in place (extra time, quiet room, reduced screen exposure, priority seating).',
        '   - Stage 4: full attendance with accommodations — gradual removal of accommodations as load is tolerated.',
        '   - Stage 5: full academic load without accommodations — return to full cognitive function confirmed.',
        '### The AEP\'s Specific Role in RTL and RTW',
        'The AEP is not the primary driver of RTL or RTW — those responsibilities sit with the GP or sports physician (medical oversight), neuropsychologist (cognitive rehabilitation), and school welfare coordinator or occupational therapist (academic or workplace accommodation). However, the AEP\'s role is specific and important:',
        '   - The athlete\'s current exercise tolerance (their HRt) is an indirect proxy for neurometabolic recovery status — a persistently low HRt suggests ongoing metabolic depression that equally constrains cognitive work.',
        '   - Coordinate session timing with the athlete\'s academic or work schedule to avoid stacking high cognitive and high physical loads in the same window.',
        '   - Communicate to the treating team when a pattern of low exercise tolerance or failure to progress the running program suggests ongoing metabolic impairment that may also be limiting RTL or RTW.',
        '   - The Amsterdam 2023 consensus endorses return to school or work — at a cognitively paced level — before and alongside return-to-sport, not after it. RTL, RTW and RTS are coordinated and concurrent, not sequential.',
        '[CALLOUT: scope | The AEP does not write RTL accommodation letters or prescribe academic adjustments — these are medical and educational decisions. Your role is to understand the cognitive-load landscape, schedule physical rehabilitation to avoid compounding cognitive exhaustion, and communicate exercise-tolerance status to the treating team in a way that informs the full return-to-activity picture.]',
        '[HIGHLIGHT: With load monitoring and cognitive pacing covered, the final section addresses objective readiness criteria and the scope-appropriate handover to the clearing clinician.]',
